Sort a list of integers
Problem statement

Sort a list in ascending order.

Input:
List<Integer> list = Arrays.asList(5, 2, 8, 1, 3);


Expected output:
[1, 2, 3, 5, 8]


A. Approach and logic
We need to arrange elements in ascending order.

In plain Java, use Collections.sort().

In Java 8, use Stream's sorted() method.
B. Plain Java
List<Integer> list = new ArrayList<>(
        Arrays.asList(5, 2, 8, 1, 3)
);

Collections.sort(list);

System.out.println(list);


C. Java 8
List<Integer> list = Arrays.asList(5, 2, 8, 1, 3);

List<Integer> result = list.stream()
        .sorted()
        .collect(Collectors.toList());

System.out.println(result);


For descending order:
List<Integer> result = list.stream()
        .sorted(Comparator.reverseOrder())
        .collect(Collectors.toList());


D. Complexity
Solution	Time	Extra space
Collections.sort	O(n log n)	O(n) implementation-dependent
Stream sorted	O(n log n)	O(n)

E. Choice of solution
Use Collections.sort() when you want to modify the original list.

Use stream().sorted() when you want to produce a separately collected result.
